  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 150 PM CST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nEnsemble and longer range guidance continues to signal a longwave \ntrough expanding over the central and eastern US through the middle \nof the week. Deterministic models are becoming confident in a \nshortwave trough sweeping through the state early Wednesday morning \nas this change in the weather pattern is ushered in. The associated \nsurface low carries precipitation (15-30% chance) and gusty winds \nwith it, but the exact magnitude, timing, and track of the low are \nstill fairly uncertain at this time. Given temperatures cooling \nWednesday night through Thursday, the potential for wintry \nprecipitation is not out of the question. The rest of the week \ncontinues this cooling trend as northerly winds amplify cold air \nadvection into the area.",
